From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yaniss <yaniss91600@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 17:32:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cuda: row-granular top-k gather in flash attention

The tile skip drops fully-masked FATTN_KQ_STRIDE tiles, so it decays with
depth: the rows a sparse top-k mask keeps scatter over more and more tiles.
Walk only the rows some query of the tile attends to instead. A prepass builds,
per Q tile, the union of those rows; the union is bounded by ncols1*top_k and
does not grow with n_kv.

gather is a template parameter, not a runtime branch. Register allocation and
occupancy are per kernel, so gather code merely present in the dense path cost
it 1-4 KB/lane of scratch and half its occupancy even when the row list was
null. The dense instantiation is now identical to before this patch (188 VGPRs,
zero scratch on <512,512,4,8>).

The row budget covers the worst case, a dense mask whose union is every KV row,
so the kernel never needs a runtime fallback. That nullable pointer, threaded
through the unrolled load path, defeated scalar-base addressing and spilled 1004
VGPRs on its own: removing it took the gather instantiation from 256 VGPRs and
4012 bytes/lane of scratch down to 131 VGPRs and zero.

Off by default, DSV4_FA_ROW_GATHER=1 to enable, =2 sabotages the row list so the
output must break. DSV4_FA_PICK_DEBUG reports which instantiation launches.

DeepSeek-V4-Flash UD-IQ3_XXS, gfx1151, -ub 2048, 2 reps, same binary:
  13884 tok: 163.9/163.4 -> 224.5/226.9 t/s  (+37.9%)
  46777 tok: 123.9/123.7 -> 205.1/204.9 t/s  (+65.7%)
Depth decay over that range goes from -24.4% to -9.2%. Greedy output is
unchanged at both depths.
